  <model metaid="meta_losartan_kidney" id="losartan_kidney" name="Model for renal excretion of losartan, E3174, and the other metabolites." substanceUnits="mmole" timeUnits="min" volumeUnits="litre" areaUnits="m2" lengthUnits="metre" extentUnits="mmole">
    <notes>
      <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <p>Model for renal excretion of losartan, E3174, and the other metabolites.</p>
        <p>
          <strong>version</strong> 2</p>
          <p>The renal clearances are given relative to the glomerular filtration rate
(GFR) and scale with the renal function (<code>f_renal_function</code>): the renal
clearance of plasma of losartan and E3174 is <code>&lt;X&gt;EX_f</code> times the
filtration of their unbound fraction in plasma (<code>fu_&lt;x&gt; * GFR</code>), the one of
the other metabolites <code>L158EX_f</code> times the GFR. The concentrations of the
kidney model are blood concentrations, the plasma concentration is the
blood concentration over the blood to plasma ratio <code>BP_&lt;x&gt;</code>.</p>
          <h2>Changelog</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>version 2</strong>
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>renal clearances relative to the GFR, plasma by the blood to plasma ratio</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            <strong>version 1</strong>
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>initial model</li>
          </ul>
          <p>The content of this model has been carefully created in a manual research effort.</p>
