    <listOfParameters>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="f_renal_function" name="renal function" value="1" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>The GFR relative to the healthy GFR <code>GFR_base</code> (101 ml/min at
75 kg): a measured creatinine clearance of X ml/min is the renal
function X/101. 1.0 is the normal renal function, below 1.0 an
impaired one.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="GFR_base" name="glomerular filtration rate (healthy)" value="101" units="ml_per_min" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="fu_los" name="fraction unbound in plasma losartan" value="0.013" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>1.3 % [Lo1995, FDA label]</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="fu_e3174" name="fraction unbound in plasma E3174" value="0.002" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>0.2 % [Lo1995, FDA label]</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="BP_los" name="blood to plasma ratio losartan" value="0.53" units="dimensionless" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="BP_e3174" name="blood to plasma ratio E3174" value="0.58" units="dimensionless" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="BP_l158" name="blood to plasma ratio other metabolites" value="1" units="dimensionless" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000009" id="LOSEX_f" name="renal clearance of unbound losartan relative to the GFR" value="59.6320404780412" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>The renal clearance of losartan is LOSEX_f times the filtration of
its unbound fraction, fu_los * GFR: 1 is filtration alone, above 1
tubular secretion. 70 ml/min of plasma [Lo1995] is about 59 (the
kidney extracts from its blood).</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
        <distrib:listOfUncertainties>
